{
  "$comment": "Explicit non-journal archive adapters; source registration remains in sources.json. HTML page/date selectors and ITDP RSS pagination verified against publisher listings on 2026-10-10. Thirty rules were added on 2026-10-15, all of them attached to sources that were already registered: `config: {}` reuses each source's own live itemSelector/publishedAtSelector, so a rule only carries the back-paginated URL shape. Every one was then re-measured on the production collector with `backfill-news.ts --max-pages=2`, and two candidates were dropped before shipping because a listing that parses on a laptop does not parse here (igg.cas.cn: 41 candidates, 37 undated; geosphere.at: 23, 15 undated) — a row without a date can never be published, so a rule that cannot date its rows is worse than no rule. `firstPage` is the number that fails silently: 1 on a CMS whose second page is index_1.html starts the walk at index_2.html and never revisits the skipped page, which is pinned by scripts/news-archive-expanded.test.ts. This is not a universal archive for all sources.",
  "archives": [
    {
      "sourceId": "rss-itdp-news",
      "mode": "pages",
      "format": "rss",
      "urlTemplate": "https://www.itdp.org/feed/?paged={page}",
      "firstPage": 1,
      "config": {}
    },
